# Voicepack — Cursor / Antigravity rules
#
# Copy this file to your project root as `.cursorrules` (or the equivalent rule
# file for your editor) and set VOICEPACK_DIR to your data directory.
#
# Replace `npx voicepack` with `node /path/to/voicepack/bin/voicepack.mjs` if you
# run from a clone instead of the published package.

## Brand voice

Whenever you write prose on behalf of this brand — social posts, captions,
threads, blog articles, newsletters, launch announcements, replies — you MUST
compile the voice pack first. Never write brand prose from memory or from a
previous turn in the conversation.

## The one rule

NEVER read the persona store directly. Do not `cat`, read, glob or grep the
data directory. It costs 8-15k tokens and makes adherence worse. The CLI reads
the store out of context and returns a pack sized to fit.

    WRONG   read $VOICEPACK_DIR/profiles/*/voice.json, rules.json, exemplars/*
    RIGHT   npx voicepack pack --profile <p> --channel <c> --intent <i>

## Procedure

1. Compile the pack:
   `npx voicepack pack --profile <p> --channel <c> --intent <i>`
   (~700 tokens). Do not skip this and do not reuse a pack from earlier.

2. Write the draft using ONLY that pack.

3. Lint it:
   `npx voicepack check --profile <p> --channel <c> --file <draft>`
   This is deterministic and offline. It catches banned lexicon, length and
   count limits, sentence and paragraph shape, punctuation, and rule regexes.

4. Judge it yourself. `check` only proves the draft is not *mechanically*
   wrong. Report two things:
   - `voiceDrift` — where it sounds like a generic AI rather than this brand.
     Cite the specific line. Look for generic CTAs, press-release openers,
     paragraphs that could belong to any company, mid-draft register shifts.
   - `keep` — what is already right and must not be touched during revision.

5. Fix only what was flagged. Do not rewrite what was not.

## Score meanings

- `ship` (>= 85) — mechanically clean
- `revise` (60-84) — fixable
- `rewrite` (< 60) — start again

A hard violation caps the score at 60 regardless of everything else.

## When the user pastes a link

    npx voicepack doctor                                       # is the bridge up?
    npx voicepack ingest --url <url> -p <p> -c <c>

Then show the user what it proposes before merging. Three rules:

- Synthesize the PATTERN, never the text. Never offer to copy phrasing.
- It lands as a candidate, not a rule. One post is one data point.
- Third-party content can never become an exemplar. The merge guard will
  refuse `--as exemplar`. Do not work around it.

If the bridge is unavailable, fall back to
`npx voicepack ingest --source <file>` with text the user pasted. Never block
the user on the bridge.

## When the user corrects a draft

A correction is a teach event, and the highest-quality signal available:

    npx voicepack teach -p <p> -c <c> --rule "..." --why "..." --strength soft

Offer to record it. Nothing is learned without the user's approval.

## Commands

    voicepack doctor
    voicepack pack    -p P -c C [-i I] [--max-tokens N]
    voicepack check   -p P -c C -f draft.md [--json] [--quiet]
    voicepack teach   -p P -c C --rule "..." [--why "..."] [--strength hard|soft]
    voicepack capture -p P -c C --url <url>
    voicepack ingest  -p P -c C [--url <url> | --capture <raw.json> | --source <file>] [--own]
    voicepack diff
    voicepack merge   -p P --id L-0001 [--as rule|hard|exemplar]
    voicepack lint    -p P   |   voicepack lint --privacy
    voicepack list
